.Dd October 27, 2026
.Dt XTC_SIM 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm xtc_sim_clock_enable ,
.Nm xtc_sim_clock_disable ,
.Nm xtc_sim_clock_advance ,
.Nm xtc_sim_clock_set ,
.Nm xtc_sim_clock_active
.Nd the deterministic simulator's virtual clock
.Sh LIBRARY
.Lb libxtc
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In xtc_sim.h
.Ft void
.Fn xtc_sim_clock_enable "int64_t start_ns"
.Ft void
.Fn xtc_sim_clock_disable "void"
.Ft void
.Fn xtc_sim_clock_advance "int64_t delta_ns"
.Ft void
.Fn xtc_sim_clock_set "int64_t ns"
.Ft int
.Fn xtc_sim_clock_active "void"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These are test seams of the deterministic simulator
.Pq Pa xtc_sim.h
is not an installed header.
While the virtual clock is enabled,
.Fn xtc_clock_mono
.Pq Xr xtc_free 3
returns virtual time, a pure function of the run's schedule, instead of
the host's monotonic clock.
.Fn xtc_sim_exec_run
enables it at time 0 for every run and disables it at the end.
.Pp
.Fn xtc_sim_clock_enable
turns the virtual clock on at
.Fa start_ns ;
.Fn xtc_sim_clock_disable
turns it off.
.Fn xtc_sim_clock_advance
moves it forward by
.Fa delta_ns ,
and
.Fn xtc_sim_clock_set
sets it to
.Fa ns .
.Pp
.Fn xtc_sim_clock_active
tells code that derives a wall-clock-like value from
.Fn xtc_clock_mono
whether it is inside a run.
Such code must not add an offset sampled from real time while the
virtual clock is active: the offset carries real time into the run, and
two runs of one seed then differ.
The determinism guard cannot see this case, because the real clock was
read before the run started.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn xtc_sim_clock_active
returns 1 while the virtual clock is enabled, else 0.
The other functions return no value.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr xtc_free 3
